      "text": "Evan Thomas, a Quaker minister, settled the land in 1745 and built a frame saw and grist mill he called Thomas’ Mill.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kemp_Mill%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1857 George Kemp bought the mill, renamed the settlement Kemp Mill, and the Kemp family ran it until 1905.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kemp_Mill%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Kemp Mill boasts creekside walkways, a calm suburban feel, Brookside Gardens, and plenty of hiking trails.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kemp_Mill%2C_Maryland"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "It hosts more than half a dozen synagogues and is home to the largest Orthodox Jewish community east of Baltimore and west of Miami.",
